reviews.body:
Definitely in the right direction! See comments, and let's make sure all the new fixtures have legit components (named correctly) that return JSX rather than this older style of test.

Also, this is missing a test where the code actually references the shadowed Symbol declaration - which, per my comment, would be incorrectly rewritten. Something like

```js
const Symbol = "<symbol>";
function Component({text}) {
  return <div>{Symbol + text}</div>
}
...fixture entrypoint...
```

